{
  "analysis": "We are at a shell prompt in /app. The task is to transcribe moves from a video of someone playing Zork and write them to /app/solution.txt. First, I need to inspect the video file and available tools for extracting frames/text from it.",
  "plan": "Run commands to list the video file, check available media/OCR tools (ffmpeg, ffprobe, tesseract), and get video metadata. This will guide how to extract frames and transcribe the text shown in the Zork game.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /app\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which ffmpeg ffprobe tesseract python3 convert 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport importlib.util\nfor m in ['cv2','PIL','numpy','easyocr','pytesseract']:\n    print(m, bool(importlib.util.find_spec(m)))\nPY\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ffprobe -v error -show_entries stream=index,codec_type,width,height,r_frame_rate,duration -show_entries format=duration -of default /app/video.mp4\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The video exists at /app/video.mp4 (~12 MB), but the initial checks show python3, ffmpeg, ffprobe, and tesseract are not installed or not on PATH. I need to identify what tools are available and potentially install or locate alternatives for extracting video frames and performing OCR.",
  "plan": "Check the OS/package manager and available interpreters/tools. Also search for Python, ffmpeg, OCR, and image utilities elsewhere on the filesystem. If apt is available, we can install needed packages.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /etc/os-release 2>/dev/null || true; echo \"PATH=$PATH\"; which apt apt-get yum apk dnf pip pip2 python python2 perl ruby convert mogrify 2>/dev/null || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -maxdepth 3 \\( -name 'ffmpeg' -o -name 'ffprobe' -o -name 'tesseract' -o -name 'python*' -o -name 'convert' -o -name 'mogrify' \\) 2>/dev/null | head -50\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /usr/bin /usr/local/bin /bin 2>/dev/null | head -200\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
